Featuring sharp, angular matte-grey plating and radar-absorbent body panels, "Sneaky" was built to blend into shadows and bypass enemy radar systems undetected. It utilized retro-reflective coating technology along with low-power acoustic repulsors, allowing Tony to fly quietly at low altitudes without triggering thermal or audio detectors.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XV plays a key moment during the House Party Protocol battle: Tony steps into "Sneaky" right after his Mark XLII falls apart. He wears it briefly to fight Aldrich Killian on the crane before Killian slices off the suit's leg, forcing Tony to eject and trigger its self-destruct mechanism.
